course: dictionary
lesson: 6534
title: Network: a web of connections
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A network is a system of lines, roads, wires or paths that cross or connect with each other. Think of a spider's web, or a map of train lines joined together. «The internet began in 1969 by linking a few computers in American universities and grew into a worldwide network.» Here network means many computers joined together, all able to reach each other.
explain: The word can also mean people. «A support network is the set of people you can turn to, such as family, teachers, the school nurse and helplines.» A support network is a group of people who are connected and help each other, not a net of wires.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The internet is a huge network that joins computers all over the world.» If you put in "a huge system of connected computers", it still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: A network is a system of connected lines, roads, wires or paths.
fact: A computer network is a group of computers connected so they can share information, like the internet.
fact: A TV or radio network is a group of stations showing the same programmes.
fact: «Network» can also be a verb: to network means to meet people who can help you, for example at work.
fact: Many apps and social networks require users to be at least 13 years old, and you should always use privacy settings.
exercise: «The internet is a huge network that joins computers all over the world.» What is a network in this sentence? | A type of bird | A small wooden box | A kind of fishing net | *A system of connected computers
exercise: Which of these is a support network? | A list of school dinners | *The people you can turn to for help, such as family and teachers | A set of buttons on a remote | A group of trees in a park
exercise: What does it mean to network? | To watch TV all day | To cut through a wire | *To meet people who can help you, for example at work | To sleep in a net
test: In «the country's network of power lines», what does network suggest? | A type of charger | A single line only | A kind of cable tie | *Many power lines joined together
test: What do the stations in a TV network show? | Different languages each day | Nothing at night | Only adverts | *The same programmes
exam: In which sentence does network mean a group of people who help each other? | The train left on time from the rail network | *Asha said her support network includes her teacher and the school nurse | Spiders spin a network of silk threads in the garden | The city has a network of roads and bridges
